Matrix correctness CI
=====================

Shared inputs use the same layout as the Vector test images:

    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/matrix/*.bin
    /nfs/share/gem5_ci/ref/matrix/riscv64-nemu-interpreter-so

The runner lists the 13 fixed-shape image filenames in matrix_ci.py. It reads
those bin files directly. No manifest, checksum file, source checkout or image
build step is needed to run CI. Missing cases are errors.

The images run one optimized xsai-blas operator with no warmup. Each contains
expected outputs from the host generic implementation. GEMM and Flash
Attention require AME+RVV; the other operators require RVV. The NEMU reference
must support the 1544-byte Matrix ABI and Matrix difftest interfaces.

The workflow runs on pushes to xs-dev and supports manual dispatch. It builds
GEM5, runs the acceptance tests and executes the suite with two parallel
simulations. Each case has a 30-minute timeout. Results and logs are uploaded
even when a case fails. The workflow builds build/RISCV_MATRIX/gem5.opt with
--enable-matrix and uses the configs/example/kmhv2_matrix.py entry point.

Run locally from the GEM5 repository root:

    scons build/RISCV_MATRIX/gem5.opt --default=RISCV --enable-matrix --linker=gold -j64
    python3 .github/workflows/autotest/script/matrix_ci.py run \
      --output /absolute/path/to/results

The build needs DRAMsim3, which the workflow prepares through
.github/actions/build-dramsim. Use --gem5 to select another Matrix-enabled
binary. Use --image-dir and --reference to override shared paths. Use
--case rms_norm to run one operator. Without --case, all 13 are required.

The runner enables --matrix and difftest, disables the instruction limit and
statistics warmup, and checks numerical correctness, normal guest completion
and completion of all Matrix checks and memory work. GEMM and Flash Attention
must each have a checked Matrix MMA. A timeout, incomplete run, fallback
implementation or numerical failure fails CI.
